{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfv2l2y9","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"chemical-equilibrium","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"chemical-equilibrium-law-of-mass-action-and-equilibrium-constant","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1--for-every-chemical-reaction-at-equilibrium-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-yi45reswxwbh8t71","content":"<p>Statement 1 : For every chemical reaction at equilibrium, standard Gibbs energy of reaction is zero.</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p>Statement 2 : At constant temperature and pressure, chemical reactions are spontaneous in the direction of decreasing Gibbs energy.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is correct explanation for Statement 1."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is NOT correct explanation for Statement 1."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True."}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>The Gibbs free energy varies from standard value as a function of temperature and equilibrium constant.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>G = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img